From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:27:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mingw: point GTK_PATH at Ardour's module directory

On Linux the ardour.sh wrapper exports GTK_PATH=@CONFDIR@:@LIBDIR@ so
that ytk loads the bundled clearlooks engine from LIBDIR/engines. The
Windows build has no wrapper script, and the upstream installer works
around it by copying clearlooks.dll to lib/gtk-2.0/engines.

When Ardour is installed into a shared prefix (e.g. an MSYS2 package)
that directory belongs to the system gtk2 and may contain a GTK2
clearlooks engine linked against libgtk-win32-2.0, which must never be
loaded into ytk. Set GTK_PATH to ardour_dll_directory() in
fixup_bundle_environment() so the engine `waf install` places in
<dll-dir>/engines is found first, mirroring the Linux wrapper.
---
 gtk2_ardour/bundle_env_mingw.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gtk2_ardour/bundle_env_mingw.cc b/gtk2_ardour/bundle_env_mingw.cc
index d4b3fbe..b5bba59 100644
--- a/gtk2_ardour/bundle_env_mingw.cc
+++ b/gtk2_ardour/bundle_env_mingw.cc
@@ -90,6 +90,20 @@ fixup_bundle_environment (int, char* [], string & localedir)
 
 	Glib::setenv ("SUIL_MODULE_DIR", Glib::build_filename(ardour_dll_directory(), "suil"), true);
 
+	/* Let ytk find Ardour's own clearlooks engine (installed as
+	 * <dll-dir>/engines/clearlooks.dll) before any GTK2 theme engine
+	 * of the same name that a system gtk2 installation may provide
+	 * in <prefix>/lib/gtk-2.0; those are linked against the real
+	 * libgtk-win32-2.0 and must not be loaded into ytk.
+	 */
+	cstr = getenv ("GTK_PATH");
+	path = ardour_dll_directory ();
+	if (cstr) {
+		path += G_SEARCHPATH_SEPARATOR;
+		path += cstr;
+	}
+	Glib::setenv ("GTK_PATH", path, true);
+
 	/* XXX this should really be PRODUCT_EXE see tools/x-win/package.sh
 	 * ardour on windows does not have a startup wrapper script.
 	 *
